// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`buildPrompt > keeps its shape (update with \`npx vitest -u\` when the template changes on purpose) 1`] = `
"Build a blog screen for a travel product using Next.js + Tailwind.

Return one complete, runnable file. Every value below is measured from a real interface, so treat it as a specification rather than a suggestion. Where the spec is silent, choose the restrained option.

The register is **editorial** — large type, wide measure, restrained colour, content-first. The target is desktop at 1440px, then tablet and mobile.

## Structure

Render these in order. The note after each is how it actually looks.

1. **Masthead** — sticky, hairline bottom border, logo lockup left, four text links, ghost sign-in plus one solid CTA on the right
2. **Lead story** — centred; small pill eyebrow, two-line headline at display size, one muted sub-line, two buttons side by side, then a large bordered product preview
3. **Article index** — rows of avatar plus two stacked lines with a right-aligned value
4. **Related grid** — three equal bordered cards; each has an accent-tinted icon square, a title, three lines of body and a small accent link
5. **Footer** — brand lockup plus four columns of links, hairline rule above

## Colour tokens

\`\`\`css
@theme {
  --color-background: #FBF7F0;
  --color-surface: #FFFDF9;
  --color-raised: #F2EADF;
  --color-border: #EADFCF;
  --color-text: #231C12;
  --color-text-muted: #87786A;
  --color-accent: #B4571F;
  --color-accent-fg: #FFF8F0;
}
\`\`\`

Reference them as \`bg-background\`, \`text-text-muted\`, \`border-border\` and so on. Do not hard-code hex values in markup.

Accent is used sparingly: primary buttons, the active navigation state, and at most one emphasis elsewhere. Everything else is neutral.

## Typography

| Step | Size | Weight | Used for |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Display | 68px | 600 | Hero headline |
| H1 | 48px | 600 | Section header |
| H2 | 38px | 600 | Sub-section |
| H3 | 22px | 560 | Card title |
| Body | 15px | 430 | Paragraph |
| Small | 13px | 450 | Meta, labels |
| Caption | 11.5px | 500 | Eyebrow, badges |

One sans-serif family throughout. Tracking tightens to about -0.028em above 40px and sits near -0.011em below it. Body line height 1.55.

## Layout and spacing

- Container: 1440px, 12 column, 24px gutters
- Radius: 8 / 12 / 16px — nothing is fully rounded except pills and avatars
- Spacing scale (4px base): 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64, 96
- Hairline borders at 1px, low contrast. Shadows only on popovers and overlays, never on cards at rest.

## Responsive behaviour

- **Masthead:** 54px, 5 sections → 44px, 5 → 32px, 4
- **Lead story:** 520px image, 46px headline → 380px, 36px → 220px, 26px
- **Article index:** 3 cards in a row → 2 × 2 → thumbnail-left list rows
- **Footer:** brand beside 4 link columns → brand above 4 columns → brand above a 2 × 2 grid

## Requirements

- Semantic landmarks: \`header\`, \`nav\`, \`main\`, \`section\`, \`footer\`
- Every interactive element keyboard reachable with a visible focus ring
- Colour contrast at least 4.5:1 for body text against its background
- Honour \`prefers-reduced-motion\`; transitions no longer than 150ms
- Explicit width and height on every image so nothing shifts as it loads
- Write plausible product copy — never lorem ipsum, never placeholder brackets

## Out of scope

- Do not reproduce any real company's name, logo, wordmark or copy. This is a structural and stylistic reference, not a brand to clone.
- No analytics, auth or data fetching unless asked — markup, styling and layout only."
`;
